This is what I originally had for rotateLeft (rotate right mirrored)
I put it together without any pseudocode or help, its how I understand a rotate happening.

The few problems I see are:
1.) It is establishing and rotating off the grand parent, not all scenario's need this
2.) It can't handle a zigzag, fixInsert was handling that in case 2
3.) This is tailored for fixInsert straight line specifically.

    private void rotateLeft(Node node) {
        // establish easier naming conventions because
        // each node points to another node
        // and the other node points back to node
        Node grand = node.parent.parent;

        //make sibling node
        Node sibling = node.parent.left;

        // set node's sibling to grandparents child
        grand.right = sibling;

        // set grandparents child to node's sibling
        // so that node no longer has a sibling
        if (sibling != null) {
            sibling.parent = grand;
        }

        // nodes sibling is now grandparent
        node.parent.left = grand;

        // set node's parent's parent to
        // node's grand parent
        node.parent.parent = grand.parent;

        // if grand was originally root
        if (grand.parent == null) {
            root = node.parent;
        }

        // see which child was the grandparent
        // set that child to be node's parent
        else if (grand == grand.parent.left) {
            grand.parent.left = node.parent;
        } else {
            grand.parent.right = node.parent;
        }

        // point grandparents parent back to node's parent
        grand.parent = node.parent;
    }